		title = "Zandalar Tribe Reputation",
		version = 1,
		why = "Shoulder and head enchants, a class necklace upgraded at every standing, and {area:19}'s set pieces.",
		written = {
			["Trash stopped counting at 11,999 Honored. Revered to Exalted is 21,000: bosses give about 1,350 a clear, and now the saved coins and bijous pay: 75 per bijou (280 bijous alone), 25 per coin set. Coins and bijous are tradeable, so the auction house is the only solo way. Each Paragons piece pays 150, each {npc:15042} enchant 100, each {item:22635} 200. Rin'wosho trades one of {npc:15042}'s potables (Spirit, Sheen or {item:20081}) for an Honor Token."] = "Trash stopped counting at 11,999 Honored. Revered to Exalted is 21,000: bosses give about 1,350 a clear, and now the saved coins and bijous pay: 75 per bijou (280 bijous alone), 25 per coin set. Coins and bijous are tradeable, so the auction house is the only solo way. Each Paragons piece pays 150, each Zanza enchant 100, each Savage Guard 200. Rin'wosho trades one of Zanza's potables (Spirit, Sheen or Swiftness of Zanza) for an Honor Token.",
			["{area:3357} is the small island off the north-west coast of {zone:1434}, west of the {area:122}: swim over from the coast. Everyone starts Neutral with the {faction:270}. {npc:15070} takes coins and bijous, {npc:14921} sells the recipes and trades Honor Tokens, and {npc:14902}, {npc:14903}, {npc:14904} and {npc:14905} hand out the class necklaces and the set pieces. Almost all Zandalar reputation comes from {area:19}, a 20-player raid, and {area:19} is not among the first raids Blizzard has announced for Forever: until it opens there is no Zandalar reputation to earn, and no coins or bijous on the auction house either. Once it is open, the only solo way is buying coins and bijous on the auction house (75 per bijou, 25 per set of three coins). The Legacy perk Diplomat adds up to 10% to every gain; the numbers in this guide are without it."] = "Yojamba Isle is the small island off the north-west coast of Stranglethorn Vale, west of the Zuuldaia Ruins: swim over from the coast. Everyone starts Neutral with the Zandalar Tribe. Vinchaxa takes coins and bijous, Rin'wosho the Trader sells the recipes and trades Honor Tokens, and Jin'rokh, Al'tabim, Maywiki and Falthir hand out the class necklaces and the set pieces. Almost all Zandalar reputation comes from Zul'Gurub, a 20-player raid, and Zul'Gurub is not among the first raids Blizzard has announced for Forever: until it opens there is no Zandalar reputation to earn, and no coins or bijous on the auction house either. Once it is open, the only solo way is buying coins and bijous on the auction house (75 per bijou, 25 per set of three coins). The Legacy perk Diplomat adds up to 10% to every gain; the numbers in this guide are without it.",
			["{npc:15042} takes an {item:18331}, Rapidity or Focus for the {item:22635} head and leg enchant: 200 reputation each, again and again. The Arcanum binds to you, so it never sells: {npc:14368} in the library of {area:2577} makes it from the matching Libram ({area:2577} drops, and on the auction house), a {item:18335} and Large Brilliant Shards, plus {item:12735}, two {item:12938} or two {item:12753}. {npc:14921} trades {quest:8196} for an Honor Token."] = "Zanza takes an Arcanum of Protection, Rapidity or Focus for the Savage Guard head and leg enchant: 200 reputation each, again and again. The Arcanum binds to you, so it never sells: Lorekeeper Lydros in the library of Dire Maul makes it from the matching Libram (Dire Maul drops, and on the auction house), a Pristine Black Diamond and Large Brilliant Shards, plus Frayed Abomination Stitching, two Blood of Heroes or two Skin of Shadow. Rin'wosho the Trader trades Essence Mangoes for an Honor Token.",
			["{npc:15042}'s enchants, from Friendly"] = "Zanza's enchants, from Friendly",
			["{npc:15042}'s head and leg enchants, from Friendly"] = "Zanza's head and leg enchants, from Friendly",
			["{npc:15042}: idol and doll, 100"] = "Zanza: idol and doll, 100",
			["{npc:15042}: {item:18329}, 200"] = "Zanza: Arcanum of Rapidity, 200",
			["{npc:15042}: {item:18330}, 200"] = "Zanza: Arcanum of Focus, 200",
			["{npc:15042}: {item:18331}, 200"] = "Zanza: Arcanum of Protection, 200",
		},
		zone = 1434,
		zoneName = "Stranglethorn Vale",
	}
end)
